    "summary": "Hooded green cloak (burnous): composed of one large piece of dyed green European cloth which is lined with four pieces of machine woven cotton dyed pink and yellow hand sewn together. The hood is edged with seven silk tassels, the neck is edged with five tassels, whilst the corners of the cloak each have a single tassel finishing them: all the tassels are dyed green. The hood is decorated with extensive embroidery in pink and green cotton forming a pattern based on a large central star. It is lined with yellow silk over which is sewn an edging of red silk which is continued round the lower border.",
